."}],"examples":["What are those? Those are lamps.","There is a lamp. → There are two lamps."]},{"question_id":"exam-ch34-v1-dialogue-where-response-assessment-transfer","content_key":"[\"sentences\",\"Where is the dining room?\",\"It is next to the kitchen.\",\"Where is the dining room? It is next to the kitchen.\",\"\",[\"It is a mirror.\",\"It is next to the kitchen.\",\"There is a table.\",\"Those are my clothes.\"],\"\",\"\"]","pattern_key":"exam-dialogue","title_th":"ฟังคำถาม แล้วจับรูปแบบคำตอบ","rule_th":"Where ถามตำแหน่ง ส่วน What is in ... ถามว่ามีอะไร ใช้ There is กับหนึ่งสิ่ง และ There are กับหลายสิ่ง","clue_th":"คำถาม Where ถามตำแหน่ง ตอบ next to the kitchen","caution_th":null,"contrasts":[{"label_th":"รูปแบบแรก","text":"Where? → On the second floor."},{"label_th":"อีกตัวอย่าง","text":"What is in the room? → There is a bed."}],"examples":["Where is the dining room? It is next to the kitchen.","There is a lamp. → There are two lamps."]},{"question_id":"exam-ch34-v1-dialogue-two-items-assessment-transfer","content_key":"[\"sentences\",\"The room has both a couch _____ an armchair.\",\"and\",\"The room has both a couch and an armchair.\",\"\",[\"and\",\"because\",\"but\",\"or\"],\"\",\"\"]","pattern_key":"exam-dialogue","title_th":"ฟังคำถาม แล้วจับรูปแบบคำตอบ","rule_th":"Where ถามตำแหน่ง ส่วน What is in ... ถามว่ามีอะไร ใช้ There is กับหนึ่งสิ่ง และ There are กับหลายสิ่ง","clue_th":"both ... and ... หมายถึงมีทั้งสองอย่าง","caution_th":null,"contrasts":[{"label_th":"รูปแบบแรก","text":"Where? → On the second floor."},{"label_th":"อีกตัวอย่าง","text":"What is in the room? → There is a bed."}],"examples":["The room has both a couch and an armchair.","There is a lamp. → There are two lamps."]},{"question_id":"exam-ch34-v1-dialogue-contracted-whats-assessment-transfer","content_key":"[\"sentences\",\"_____ in the living room? There are two armchairs.\",\"What’s\",\"What’s in the living room? There are two armchairs.\",\"\",[\"What’s\",\"When’s\",\"Where’s\",\"Who’s\"],\"\",\"\"]","pattern_key":"exam-dialogue","title_th":"ฟังคำถาม แล้วจับรูปแบบคำตอบ","rule_th":"Where ถามตำแหน่ง ส่วน What is in ... ถามว่ามีอะไร ใช้ There is กับหนึ่งสิ่ง และ There are กับหลายสิ่ง","clue_th":"What’s in ถามว่ามีอะไร แม้คำตอบมีหลายชิ้นก็ถามแบบนี้ได้","caution_th":null,"contrasts":[{"label_th":"รูปแบบแรก","text":"Where? → On the second floor."},{"label_th":"อีกตัวอย่าง","text":"What is in the room? → There is a bed."}],"examples":["What’s in the living room? There are two armchairs.","There is a lamp. → There are two lamps."]},{"question_id":"exam-ch34-v1-reading-houses-main-practice-transfer","content_key":"[\"sentences\",\"Which title best fits this paragraph?\",\"Places people call home.\",\"Which title best fits this paragraph? Places people call home.\",\"\",[\"A school timetable.\",\"Cooking at home.\",\"How to catch a train.\",\"Places people call home.\"],\"Fifty-six percent of the world’s people live in cities. Many people in the city live in apartments. Others live around cities, in smaller towns called suburbs. There are many houses in the suburbs. Outside of cities and suburbs is the countryside. The countryside has a lot of space, so there are big houses and even farms. Houses, apartments, and farms are not the only places where people live. Some people live in really different houses!\",\"\"]","pattern_key":"exam-reading","title_th":"หาหลักฐานในข้อความ","rule_th":"อ่านคำถามว่าถามใคร ที่ไหน จำนวน วิธี หรือความหมาย แล้วหาใจความที่ตอบเรื่องเดียวกันในข้อความ","clue_th":"ดูใจความที่ครอบคลุมบ้านและที่อยู่อาศัยหลายรูปแบบ","caution_th":null,"contrasts":[{"label_th":"รูปแบบแรก","text":"Where? → a place"},{"label_th":"อีกตัวอย่าง","text":"How many? → a number"}],"examples":["Which title best fits this paragraph? Places people call home.","Where is the house? → In Serbia."]},{"question_id":"exam-ch34-v1-reading-houses-suburbs-practice-transfer","content_key":"[\"sentences\",\"What are the smaller towns around cities called?\",\"Suburbs.\",\"What are the smaller towns around cities called? Suburbs.\",\"\",[\"Caves.\",\"Platforms.\",\"Suburbs.\",\"Treehouses.\"],\"Fifty-six percent of the world’s people live in cities. Many people in the city live in apartments. Others live around cities, in smaller towns called suburbs. There are many houses in the suburbs. Outside of cities and suburbs is the countryside. The countryside has a lot of space, so there are big houses and even farms. Houses, apartments, and farms are not the only places where people live. Some people live in really different houses!\",\"\"]","pattern_key":"exam-reading","title_th":"หาหลักฐานในข้อความ","rule_th":"อ่านคำถามว่าถามใคร ที่ไหน จำนวน วิธี หรือความหมาย แล้วหาใจความที่ตอบเรื่องเดียวกันในข้อความ","clue_th":"called suburbs บอกชื่อเมืองเล็กรอบเมืองใหญ่","caution_th":null,"contrasts":[{"label_th":"รูปแบบแรก","text":"Where? → a place"},{"label_th":"อีกตัวอย่าง","text":"How many? → a number"}],"examples":["What are the smaller towns around cities called? Suburbs.","Where is the house? → In Serbia."]},{"question_id":"exam-ch34-v1-reading-houses-serbia-practice-transfer","content_key":"[\"sentences\",\"Which country has the house over the Drina River?\",\"Serbia.\",\"Which country has the house over the Drina River? Serbia.\",\"\",[\"Indonesia.\",\"Japan.\",\"Serbia.\",\"Turkey.\"],\"The Drina River house is not a house beside the water. It’s a house over the water! This house is in Serbia. People love to visit and take photographs of it.\",\"\"]","pattern_key":"exam-reading","title_th":"หาหลักฐานในข้อความ","rule_th":"อ่านคำถามว่าถามใคร ที่ไหน จำนวน วิธี หรือความหมาย แล้วหาใจความที่ตอบเรื่องเดียวกันในข้อความ","clue_th":"This house ย้อนถึงบ้านเหนือแม่น้ำที่กล่าวก่อนหน้า อยู่ใน Serbia","caution_th":null,"contrasts":[{"label_th":"รูปแบบแรก","text":"Where? → a place"},{"label_th":"อีกตัวอย่าง","text":"How many? → a number"}],"examples":["Which country has the house over the Drina River? Serbia.","Where is the house? → In Serbia."]},{"question_id":"exam-ch34-v1-reading-houses-treehouses-practice-transfer","content_key":"[\"sentences\",\"What is near the three treehouses?\",\"Diamond Beach.\",\"What is near the three treehouses? Diamond Beach.\",\"\",[\"A subway platform.\",\"Diamond Beach.\",\"The Drina River.\",\"The city center of Chicago.\"],\"Treehouses are a lot of fun, but do you want to live in one? In Bali, Indonesia, you can try living in the famous Rumah Pohon Treehouse. There are three treehouses there that you can stay in. They are near the beautiful Diamond Beach.\",\"\"]","pattern_key":"exam-reading","title_th":"หาหลักฐานในข้อความ","rule_th":"อ่านคำถามว่าถามใคร ที่ไหน จำนวน วิธี หรือความหมาย แล้วหาใจความที่ตอบเรื่องเดียวกันในข้อความ","clue_th":"They อ้างถึงบ้านต้นไม้ ส่วน near Diamond Beach บอกว่าอยู่ใกล้ชายหาด","caution_th":null,"contrasts":[{"label_th":"รูปแบบแรก","text":"Where? → a place"},{"label_th":"อีกตัวอย่าง","text":"How many? → a number"}],"examples":["What is near the three treehouses? Diamond Beach.","Where is the house? → In Serbia."]},{"question_id":"exam-ch34-v1-reading-houses-rocks-practice-transfer","content_key":"[\"sentences\",\"Where did people make the cave houses?\",\"Inside large rocks.\",\"Where did people make the cave houses? Inside large rocks.\",\"\",[\"Inside buses.\",\"Inside large rocks.\",\"On train platforms.\",\"Under the sea.\"],\"In Cappadocia, Turkey, you can find very different houses! Cappadocia has many cave houses. People made them inside large rocks. The rocks in Cappadocia are kind of soft. People have lived in these cave homes for thousands of years.\",\"\"]","pattern_key":"exam-reading","title_th":"หาหลักฐานในข้อความ","rule_th":"อ่านคำถามว่าถามใคร ที่ไหน จำนวน วิธี หรือความหมาย แล้วหาใจความที่ตอบเรื่องเดียวกันในข้อความ","clue_th":"People made them inside large rocks บอกตำแหน่งที่สร้างบ้านถ้ำ","caution_th":null,"contrasts":[{"label_th":"รูปแบบแรก","text":"Where? → a place"},{"label_th":"อีกตัวอย่าง","text":"How many? → a number"}],"examples":["Where did people make the cave houses? Inside large rocks.","Where is the house? → In Serbia."]},{"question_id":"exam-ch34-v1-reading-train-name-practice-transfer","content_key":"[\"sentences\",\"In this passage, what does “the L” name?\",\"An overhead train.\",\"In this passage, what does “the L” name? An overhead train.\",\"\",[\"A beach.\",\"A cave house.\",\"A taxi company.\",\"An overhead train.\"],\"In Chicago, the overhead train is called the L. The tracks make a loop around the city center and then run out in all directions to the different parts of the city. The tracks are supported by massive steel columns.\",\"\"]","pattern_key":"exam-reading","title_th":"หาหลักฐานในข้อความ","rule_th":"อ่านคำถามว่าถามใคร ที่ไหน จำนวน วิธี หรือความหมาย แล้วหาใจความที่ตอบเรื่องเดียวกันในข้อความ","clue_th":"the overhead train is called the L บอกชื่อรถไฟ","caution_th":null,"contrasts":[{"label_th":"รูปแบบแรก","text":"Where? → a place"},{"label_th":"อีกตัวอย่าง","text":"How many? → a number"}],"examples":["In this passage, what does “the L” name? An overhead train.","Where is the house? → In Serbia."]},{"question_id":"exam-ch34-v1-reading-train-support-practice-transfer","content_key":"[\"sentences\",\"What material are the supporting columns made of?\",\"Steel.\",\"What material are the supporting columns made of? Steel.\",\"\",[\"Glass.\",\"Paper.\",\"Steel.\",\"Wood.\"],\"In Chicago, the overhead train is called the L. The tracks make a loop around the city center and then run out in all directions to the different parts of the city. The tracks are supported by massive steel columns.\",\"\"]","pattern_key":"exam-reading","title_th":"หาหลักฐานในข้อความ","rule_th":"อ่านคำถามว่าถามใคร ที่ไหน จำนวน วิธี หรือความหมาย แล้วหาใจความที่ตอบเรื่องเดียวกันในข้อความ","clue_th":"steel ขยาย columns บอกวัสดุของเสาที่รองรับราง","caution_th":null,"contrasts":[{"label_th":"รูปแบบแรก","text":"Where? → a place"},{"label_th":"อีกตัวอย่าง","text":"How many? → a number"}],"examples":["What material are the supporting columns made of? Steel.","Where is the house? → In Serbia."]},{"question_id":"exam-ch34-v1-reading-train-platform-practice-transfer","content_key":"[\"sentences\",\"Where do riders go using stairs or an elevator?\",\"The platform.\",\"Where do riders go using stairs or an elevator? The platform.\",\"\",[\"A treehouse.\",\"Diamond Beach.\",\"Inside a taxi.\",\"The platform.\"],\"Riding the train is easy. Riders climb stairs or take an elevator from the sidewalk to the platform. They buy a ticket, go through a gate, and wait for the next train to take them where they want to go. A train ticket costs less than a taxi ride. At busy times, trains come as often as every ten minutes. At night and on weekends, they do not come as often. Some trains run all the time, day or night.\",\"\"]","pattern_key":"exam-reading","title_th":"หาหลักฐานในข้อความ","rule_th":"อ่านคำถามว่าถามใคร ที่ไหน จำนวน วิธี หรือความหมาย แล้วหาใจความที่ตอบเรื่องเดียวกันในข้อความ","clue_th":"from ... to ... บอกจุดเริ่มต้นและปลายทาง ปลายทางคือ platform","caution_th":null,"contrasts":[{"label_th":"รูปแบบแรก","text":"Where? → a place"},{"label_th":"อีกตัวอย่าง","text":"How many? → a number"}],"examples":["Where do riders go using stairs or an elevator? The platform.","Where is the house? → In Serbia."]},{"question_id":"exam-ch34-v1-reading-train-price-practice-transfer","content_key":"[\"sentences\",\"Which journey is more expensive in the passage?\",\"A taxi ride.\",\"Which journey is more expensive in the passage? A taxi ride.\",\"\",[\"A taxi ride.\",\"A train ride.\",\"Both are free.\",\"Both cost the same.\"],\"Riding the train is easy. Riders climb stairs or take an elevator from the sidewalk to the platform. They buy a ticket, go through a gate, and wait for the next train to take them where they want to go. A train ticket costs less than a taxi ride. At busy times, trains come as often as every ten minutes. At night and on weekends, they do not come as often. Some trains run all the time, day or night.\",\"\"]","pattern_key":"exam-reading","title_th":"หาหลักฐานในข้อความ","rule_th":"อ่านคำถามว่าถามใคร ที่ไหน จำนวน วิธี หรือความหมาย แล้วหาใจความที่ตอบเรื่องเดียวกันในข้อความ","clue_th":"รถไฟ costs less than taxi แปลว่ารถแท็กซี่แพงกว่า","caution_th":null,"contrasts":[{"label_th":"รูปแบบแรก","text":"Where? → a place"},{"label_th":"อีกตัวอย่าง","text":"How many? → a number"}],"examples":["Which journey is more expensive in the passage? A taxi ride.","Where is the house? → In Serbia."]},{"question_id":"exam-ch34-v1-reading-train-frequency-practice-transfer","content_key":"[\"sentences\",\"Which period has more frequent trains?\",\"Busy times.\",\"Which period has more frequent trains? Busy times.\",\"\",[\"All periods are equally frequent.\",\"Busy times.\",\"Nighttime.\",\"Weekends.\"],\"Riding the train is easy. Riders climb stairs or take an elevator from the sidewalk to the platform. They buy a ticket, go through a gate, and wait for the next train to take them where they want to go. A train ticket costs less than a taxi ride. At busy times, trains come as often as every ten minutes. At night and on weekends, they do not come as often. Some trains run all the time, day or night.\",\"\"]","pattern_key":"exam-reading","title_th":"หาหลักฐานในข้อความ","rule_th":"อ่านคำถามว่าถามใคร ที่ไหน จำนวน วิธี หรือความหมาย แล้วหาใจความที่ตอบเรื่องเดียวกันในข้อความ","clue_th":"not as often ตอนกลางคืนและสุดสัปดาห์แปลว่าช่วงคนมากรถไฟถี่กว่า","caution_th":null,"contrasts":[{"label_th":"รูปแบบแรก","text":"Where? → a place"},{"label_th":"อีกตัวอย่าง","text":"How many? → a number"}],"examples":["Which period has more frequent trains? Busy times.","Where is the house? → In Serbia."]},{"question_id":"exam-ch34-v1-reading-houses-percent-practice-transfer","content_key":"[\"sentences\",\"Where do many city residents live?\",\"In apartments.\",\"Where do many city residents live? In apartments.\",\"\",[\"In apartments.\",\"On train tracks.\",\"Only in caves.\",\"Only on farms.\"],\"Fifty-six percent of the world’s people live in cities. Many people in the city live in apartments. Others live around cities, in smaller towns called suburbs. There are many houses in the suburbs. Outside of cities and suburbs is the countryside. The countryside has a lot of space, so there are big houses and even farms. Houses, apartments, and farms are not the only places where people live. Some people live in really different houses!\",\"\"]","pattern_key":"exam-reading","title_th":"หาหลักฐานในข้อความ","rule_th":"อ่านคำถามว่าถามใคร ที่ไหน จำนวน วิธี หรือความหมาย แล้วหาใจความที่ตอบเรื่องเดียวกันในข้อความ","clue_th":"Many people in the city live in apartments เป็นหลักฐานตรง","caution_th":null,"contrasts":[{"label_th":"รูปแบบแรก","text":"Where? → a place"},{"label_th":"อีกตัวอย่าง","text":"How many? → a number"}],"examples":["Where do many city residents live? In apartments.","Where is the house? → In Serbia."]},{"question_id":"exam-ch34-v1-reading-houses-space-practice-transfer","content_key":"[\"sentences\",\"Which place has enough space for big houses and farms?\",\"The countryside.\",\"Which place has enough space for big houses and farms? The countryside.\",\"\",[\"A small elevator.\",\"A train platform.\",\"Inside a taxi.\",\"The countryside.\"],\"Fifty-six percent of the world’s people live in cities. Many people in the city live in apartments. Others live around cities, in smaller towns called suburbs. There are many houses in the suburbs. Outside of cities and suburbs is the countryside. The countryside has a lot of space, so there are big houses and even farms. Houses, apartments, and farms are not the only places where people live. Some people live in really different houses!\",\"\"]","pattern_key":"exam-reading","title_th":"หาหลักฐานในข้อความ","rule_th":"อ่านคำถามว่าถามใคร ที่ไหน จำนวน วิธี หรือความหมาย แล้วหาใจความที่ตอบเรื่องเดียวกันในข้อความ","clue_th":"The countryside has a lot of space บอกเหตุที่มีบ้านใหญ่และฟาร์ม","caution_th":null,"contrasts":[{"label_th":"รูปแบบแรก","text":"Where? → a place"},{"label_th":"อีกตัวอย่าง","text":"How many? → a number"}],"examples":["Which place has enough space for big houses and farms? The countryside.","Where is the house? → In Serbia."]},{"question_id":"exam-ch34-v1-reading-houses-water-practice-transfer","content_key":"[\"sentences\",\"Which description does the passage explicitly reject?\",\"The house is beside the water.\",\"Which description does the passage explicitly reject? The house is beside the water.\",\"\",[\"It is a house.\",\"The house exists.\",\"The house is beside the water.\",\"The house is over the water.\"],\"The Drina River house is not a house beside the water. It’s a house over the water! This house is in Serbia. People love to visit and take photographs of it.\",\"\"]","pattern_key":"exam-reading","title_th":"หาหลักฐานในข้อความ","rule_th":"อ่านคำถามว่าถามใคร ที่ไหน จำนวน วิธี หรือความหมาย แล้วหาใจความที่ตอบเรื่องเดียวกันในข้อความ","clue_th":"not a house beside the water ปฏิเสธตำแหน่ง beside","caution_th":null,"contrasts":[{"label_th":"รูปแบบแรก","text":"Where? → a place"},{"label_th":"อีกตัวอย่าง","text":"How many? → a number"}],"examples":["Which description does the passage explicitly reject? The house is beside the water.","Where is the house? → In Serbia."]},{"question_id":"exam-ch34-v1-reading-houses-bali-practice-transfer","content_key":"[\"sentences\",\"In which country is Bali in this passage?\",\"Indonesia.\",\"In which country is Bali in this passage? Indonesia.\",\"\",[\"Indonesia.\",\"Japan.\",\"Serbia.\",\"Turkey.\"],\"Treehouses are a lot of fun, but do you want to live in one? In Bali, Indonesia, you can try living in the famous Rumah Pohon Treehouse. There are three treehouses there that you can stay in. They are near the beautiful Diamond Beach.\",\"\"]","pattern_key":"exam-reading","title_th":"หาหลักฐานในข้อความ","rule_th":"อ่านคำถามว่าถามใคร ที่ไหน จำนวน วิธี หรือความหมาย แล้วหาใจความที่ตอบเรื่องเดียวกันในข้อความ","clue_th":"Bali, Indonesia ใช้ชื่อประเทศขยายชื่อสถานที่","caution_th":null,"contrasts":[{"label_th":"รูปแบบแรก","text":"Where? → a place"},{"label_th":"อีกตัวอย่าง","text":"How many? → a number"}],"examples":["In which country is Bali in this passage? Indonesia.","Where is the house? → In Serbia."]},{"question_id":"exam-ch34-v1-reading-houses-soft-practice-transfer","content_key":"[\"sentences\",\"Which description matches the rocks in Cappadocia?\",\"They are kind of soft.\",\"Which description matches the rocks in Cappadocia? They are kind of soft.\",\"\",[\"They are all underwater.\",\"They are kind of soft.\",\"They are made of steel.\",\"They are train tracks.\"],\"In Cappadocia, Turkey, you can find very different houses! Cappadocia has many cave houses. People made them inside large rocks. The rocks in Cappadocia are kind of soft. People have lived in these cave homes for thousands of years.\",\"\"]","pattern_key":"exam-reading","title_th":"หาหลักฐานในข้อความ","rule_th":"อ่านคำถามว่าถามใคร ที่ไหน จำนวน วิธี หรือความหมาย แล้วหาใจความที่ตอบเรื่องเดียวกันในข้อความ","clue_th":"The rocks ... are kind of soft บอกลักษณะหิน","caution_th":null,"contrasts":[{"label_th":"รูปแบบแรก","text":"Where? → a place"},{"label_th":"อีกตัวอย่าง","text":"How many? → a number"}],"examples":["Which description matches the rocks in Cappadocia? They are kind of soft.","Where is the house? → In Serbia."]},{"question_id":"exam-ch34-v1-reading-houses-years-practice-transfer","content_key":"[\"sentences\",\"Have people used these cave homes only recently?\",\"No, for thousands of years.\",\"Have people used these cave homes only recently? No, for thousands of years.\",\"\",[\"No one has lived there.\",\"No, for thousands of years.\",\"Yes, for ten minutes.\",\"Yes, since yesterday.\"],\"In Cappadocia, Turkey, you can find very different houses! Cappadocia has many cave houses. People made them inside large rocks. The rocks in Cappadocia are kind of soft. People have lived in these cave homes for thousands of years.\",\"\"]","pattern_key":"exam-reading","title_th":"หาหลักฐานในข้อความ","rule_th":"อ่านคำถามว่าถามใคร ที่ไหน จำนวน วิธี หรือความหมาย แล้วหาใจความที่ตอบเรื่องเดียวกันในข้อความ","clue_th":"for thousands of years หมายถึงระยะเวลายาวนาน ไม่ใช่เพิ่งเริ่ม","caution_th":null,"contrasts":[{"label_th":"รูปแบบแรก","text":"Where? → a place"},{"label_th":"อีกตัวอย่าง","text":"How many? → a number"}],"examples":["Have people used these cave homes only recently? No, for thousands of years.","Where is the house? → In Serbia."]},{"question_id":"exam-ch34-v1-reading-train-noise-practice-transfer","content_key":"[\"sentences\",\"Why does the writer tell the reader to look up?\",\"A train is passing overhead.\",\"Why does the writer tell the reader to look up? A train is passing overhead.\",\"\",[\"A bus is in a cave.\",\"A taxi is underground.\",\"A train is passing overhead.\",\"It is raining heavily.\"],\"The sun is shining, but you think you hear thunder. Look up! A train is passing over your head!\",\"\"]","pattern_key":"exam-reading","title_th":"หาหลักฐานในข้อความ","rule_th":"อ่านคำถามว่าถามใคร ที่ไหน จำนวน วิธี หรือความหมาย แล้วหาใจความที่ตอบเรื่องเดียวกันในข้อความ","clue_th":"Look up ตามด้วยรถไฟผ่านเหนือหัว เป็นเหตุให้มองขึ้น","caution_th":null,"contrasts":[{"label_th":"รูปแบบแรก","text":"Where? → a place"},{"label_th":"อีกตัวอย่าง","text":"How many? → a number"}],"examples":["Why does the writer tell the reader to look up? A train is passing overhead.","Where is the house? → In Serbia."]},{"question_id":"exam-ch34-v1-reading-train-traffic-practice-transfer","content_key":"[\"sentences\",\"What happens to cars and buses on the ground?\",\"They start and stop in traffic.\",\"What happens to cars and buses on the ground? They start and stop in traffic.\",\"\",[\"They fly over the trains.\",\"They never stop.\",\"They start and stop in traffic.\",\"They use the train tracks.\"],\"Some big cities build train tracks above the city streets. One of these cities is Chicago. On the ground, cars and buses start and stop in traffic. Above them, trains are moving from station to station with no traffic jams.\",\"\"]","pattern_key":"exam-reading","title_th":"หาหลักฐานในข้อความ","rule_th":"อ่านคำถามว่าถามใคร ที่ไหน จำนวน วิธี หรือความหมาย แล้วหาใจความที่ตอบเรื่องเดียวกันในข้อความ","clue_th":"On the ground บอกจุดเปรียบเทียบกับรถไฟด้านบน","caution_th":null,"contrasts":[{"label_th":"รูปแบบแรก","text":"Where? → a place"},{"label_th":"อีกตัวอย่าง","text":"How many? → a number"}],"examples":["What happens to cars and buses on the ground? They start and stop in traffic.","Where is the house? → In Serbia."]},{"question_id":"exam-ch34-v1-reading-train-loop-practice-transfer","content_key":"[\"sentences\",\"What shape do the tracks make around the city center?\",\"A loop.\",\"What shape do the tracks make around the city center? A loop.\",\"\",[\"A loop.\",\"A roof.\",\"A staircase.\",\"A wall.\"],\"In Chicago, the overhead train is called the L. The tracks make a loop around the city center and then run out in all directions to the different parts of the city. The tracks are supported by massive steel columns.\",\"\"]","pattern_key":"exam-reading","title_th":"หาหลักฐานในข้อความ","rule_th":"อ่านคำถามว่าถามใคร ที่ไหน จำนวน วิธี หรือความหมาย แล้วหาใจความที่ตอบเรื่องเดียวกันในข้อความ","clue_th":"make a loop around บอกรูปร่างเส้นทางวนรอบ","caution_th":null,"contrasts":[{"label_th":"รูปแบบแรก","text":"Where? → a place"},{"label_th":"อีกตัวอย่าง","text":"How many? → a number"}],"examples":["What shape do the tracks make around the city center? A loop.","Where is the house? → In Serbia."]},{"question_id":"exam-ch34-v1-reading-train-sequence-practice-transfer","content_key":"[\"sentences\",\"What do riders do first in this sequence?\",\"Buy a ticket.\",\"What do riders do first in this sequence? Buy a ticket.\",\"\",[\"Buy a ticket.\",\"Go through the gate.\",\"Reach their stop.\",\"Wait for the next train.\"],\"Riding the train is easy. Riders climb stairs or take an elevator from the sidewalk to the platform. They buy a ticket, go through a gate, and wait for the next train to take them where they want to go. A train ticket costs less than a taxi ride. At busy times, trains come as often as every ten minutes. At night and on weekends, they do not come as often. Some trains run all the time, day or night.\",\"\"]","pattern_key":"exam-reading","title_th":"หาหลักฐานในข้อความ","rule_th":"อ่านคำถามว่าถามใคร ที่ไหน จำนวน วิธี หรือความหมาย แล้วหาใจความที่ตอบเรื่องเดียวกันในข้อความ","clue_th":"รายการการกระทำเรียง buy a ticket ก่อน go through a gate และ wait","caution_th":null,"contrasts":[{"label_th":"รูปแบบแรก","text":"Where? → a place"},{"label_th":"อีกตัวอย่าง","text":"How many? → a number"}],"examples":["What do riders do first in this sequence? Buy a ticket.","Where is the house? → In Serbia."]},{"question_id":"exam-ch34-v1-reading-train-busy-practice-transfer","content_key":"[\"sentences\",\"Which interval is stated for busy times?\",\"Ten minutes.\",\"Which interval is stated for busy times? Ten minutes.\",\"\",[\"Fifty-six hours.\",\"One month.\",\"Ten days.\",\"Ten minutes.\"],\"Riding the train is easy. Riders climb stairs or take an elevator from the sidewalk to the platform. They buy a ticket, go through a gate, and wait for the next train to take them where they want to go. A train ticket costs less than a taxi ride. At busy times, trains come as often as every ten minutes. At night and on weekends, they do not come as often. Some trains run all the time, day or night.\",\"\"]","pattern_key":"exam-reading","title_th":"หาหลักฐานในข้อความ","rule_th":"อ่านคำถามว่าถามใคร ที่ไหน จำนวน วิธี หรือความหมาย แล้วหาใจความที่ตอบเรื่องเดียวกันในข้อความ","clue_th":"every ten minutes คือช่วงห่างสิบนาที","caution_th":null,"contrasts":[{"label_th":"รูปแบบแรก","text":"Where? → a place"},{"label_th":"อีกตัวอย่าง","text":"How many? → a number"}],"examples":["Which interval is stated for busy times? Ten minutes.","Where is the house? → In Serbia."]},{"question_id":"exam-ch34-v1-reading-train-students-practice-transfer","content_key":"[\"sentences\",\"What can students use their phones for on the train?\",\"Playing a game.\",\"What can students use their phones for on the train? Playing a game.\",\"\",[\"Building tracks.\",\"Cooking a meal.\",\"Driving the train.\",\"Playing a game.\"],\"While drivers on the ground are stuck in traffic, riders on the L are on their way. Students can do their homework or play a game on their phone. People read or talk. Some even go to sleep and wake up when they reach their stop.\",\"\"]","pattern_key":"exam-reading","title_th":"หาหลักฐานในข้อความ","rule_th":"อ่านคำถามว่าถามใคร ที่ไหน จำนวน วิธี หรือความหมาย แล้วหาใจความที่ตอบเรื่องเดียวกันในข้อความ","clue_th":"play a game on their phone เป็นกิจกรรมที่ระบุในเรื่อง","caution_th":null,"contrasts":[{"label_th":"รูปแบบแรก","text":"Where? → a place"},{"label_th":"อีกตัวอย่าง","text":"How many? → a number"}],"examples":["What can students use their phones for on the train? Playing a game.","Where is the house? → In Serbia."]},{"question_id":"exam-ch34-v1-reading-train-some-practice-transfer","content_key":"[\"sentences\",\"Does the passage say every train runs all day and night?\",\"No, it says some trains.\",\"Does the passage say every train runs all day and night? No, it says some trains.\",\"\",[\"It says no trains.\",\"It says only taxis.\",\"No, it says some trains.\",\"Yes, every train.\"],\"Riding the train is easy. Riders climb stairs or take an elevator from the sidewalk to the platform. They buy a ticket, go through a gate, and wait for the next train to take them where they want to go. A train ticket costs less than a taxi ride. At busy times, trains come as often as every ten minutes. At night and on weekends, they do not come as often. Some trains run all the time, day or night.\",\"\"]","pattern_key":"exam-reading","title_th":"หาหลักฐานในข้อความ","rule_th":"อ่านคำถามว่าถามใคร ที่ไหน จำนวน วิธี หรือความหมาย แล้วหาใจความที่ตอบเรื่องเดียวกันในข้อความ","clue_th":"Some ไม่ได้แปลว่า all ห้ามขยายคำกล่าวเกินหลักฐาน","caution_th":null,"contrasts":[{"label_th":"รูปแบบแรก","text":"Where? → a place"},{"label_th":"อีกตัวอย่าง","text":"How many? → a number"}],"examples":["Does the passage say every train runs all day and night? No, it says some trains.","Where is the house? → In Serbia."]},{"question_id":"exam-ch34-v1-reading-train-main-practice-transfer","content_key":"[\"sentences\",\"Which contrast is central to this paragraph?\",\"Road traffic stops drivers while train riders keep travelling.\",\"Which contrast is central to this paragraph? Road traffic stops drivers while train riders keep travelling.\",\"\",[\"All passengers drive cars.\",\"Road traffic stops drivers while train riders keep travelling.\",\"Students cannot use trains.\",\"Trains are always stuck behind buses.\"],\"While drivers on the ground are stuck in traffic, riders on the L are on their way. Students can do their homework or play a game on their phone. People read or talk. Some even go to sleep and wake up when they reach their stop.\",\"\"]","pattern_key":"exam-reading","title_th":"หาหลักฐานในข้อความ","rule_th":"อ่านคำถามว่าถามใคร ที่ไหน จำนวน วิธี หรือความหมาย แล้วหาใจความที่ตอบเรื่องเดียวกันในข้อความ","clue_th":"While เชื่อมสถานการณ์ต่างกัน: รถติดด้านล่างแต่ผู้โดยสารรถไฟยังเดินทาง","caution_th":null,"contrasts":[{"label_th":"รูปแบบแรก","text":"Where? → a place"},{"label_th":"อีกตัวอย่าง","text":"How many? → a number"}],"examples":["Which contrast is central to this paragraph? Road traffic stops drivers while train riders keep travelling.","Where is the house? → In Serbia."]},{"question_id":"exam-ch34-v1-reading-houses-main-assessment-transfer","content_key":"[\"sentences\",\"Which idea is supported by the paragraph as a whole?\",\"People live in several kinds of places.\",\"Which idea is supported by the paragraph as a whole? People live in several kinds of places.\",\"\",[\"All houses are in cities.\",\"Everyone lives on a farm.\",\"Nobody lives in apartments.\",\"People live in several kinds of places.\"],\"Fifty-six percent of the world’s people live in cities. Many people in the city live in apartments. Others live around cities, in smaller towns called suburbs. There are many houses in the suburbs. Outside of cities and suburbs is the countryside. The countryside has a lot of space, so there are big houses and even farms. Houses, apartments, and farms are not the only places where people live. Some people live in really different houses!\",\"\"]","pattern_key":"exam-reading","title_th":"หาหลักฐานในข้อความ","rule_th":"อ่านคำถามว่าถามใคร ที่ไหน จำนวน วิธี หรือความหมาย แล้วหาใจความที่ตอบเรื่องเดียวกันในข้อความ","clue_th":"ดูภาพรวม บ้านมีหลายชนิด ไม่เลือกคำกล่าวที่ใช้ everyone หรือ all เกินข้อความ","caution_th":null,"contrasts":[{"label_th":"รูปแบบแรก","text":"Where? → a place"},{"label_th":"อีกตัวอย่าง","text":"How many? → a number"}],"examples":["Which idea is supported by the paragraph as a whole? People live in several kinds of places.","Where is the house? → In Serbia."]},{"question_id":"exam-ch34-v1-reading-houses-suburbs-assessment-transfer","content_key":"[\"sentences\",\"A family lives in a small town around a city. Which term fits the passage?\",\"A suburb.\",\"A family lives in a small town around a city. Which term fits the passage? A suburb.\",\"\",[\"A platform.\",\"A railway.\",\"A suburb.\",\"A treehouse.\"],\"Fifty-six percent of the world’s people live in cities. Many people in the city live in apartments. Others live around cities, in smaller towns called suburbs. There are many houses in the suburbs. Outside of cities and suburbs is the countryside. The countryside has a lot of space, so there are big houses and even farms. Houses, apartments, and farms are not the only places where people live. Some people live in really different houses!\",\"\"]","pattern_key":"exam-reading","title_th":"หาหลักฐานในข้อความ","rule_th":"อ่านคำถามว่าถามใคร ที่ไหน จำนวน วิธี หรือความหมาย แล้วหาใจความที่ตอบเรื่องเดียวกันในข้อความ","clue_th":"ใช้คำอธิบาย smaller towns around cities กับตัวอย่างใหม่ คือ suburb","caution_th":null,"contrasts":[{"label_th":"รูปแบบแรก","text":"Where? → a place"},{"label_th":"อีกตัวอย่าง","text":"How many? → a number"}],"examples":["A family lives in a small town around a city. Which term fits the passage? A suburb.","Where is the house? → In Serbia."]},{"question_id":"exam-ch34-v1-reading-houses-serbia-assessment-transfer","content_key":"[\"sentences\",\"A visitor wants to photograph the Drina River house. Which country should they visit?\",\"Serbia.\",\"A visitor wants to photograph the Drina River house. Which country should they visit? Serbia.\",\"\",[\"Indonesia.\",\"Japan.\",\"Serbia.\",\"Turkey.\"],\"The Drina River house is not a house beside the water. It’s a house over the water! This house is in Serbia. People love to visit and take photographs of it.\",\"\"]","pattern_key":"exam-reading","title_th":"หาหลักฐานในข้อความ","rule_th":"อ่านคำถามว่าถามใคร ที่ไหน จำนวน วิธี หรือความหมาย แล้วหาใจความที่ตอบเรื่องเดียวกันในข้อความ","clue_th":"ตามชื่อบ้าน Drina River house ไปยัง This house is in Serbia","caution_th":null,"contrasts":[{"label_th":"รูปแบบแรก","text":"Where? → a place"},{"label_th":"อีกตัวอย่าง","text":"How many? → a number"}],"examples":["A visitor wants to photograph the Drina River house. Which country should they visit? Serbia.","Where is the house? → In Serbia."]},{"question_id":"exam-ch34-v1-reading-houses-treehouses-assessment-transfer","content_key":"[\"sentences\",\"In “They are near the beautiful Diamond Beach”, what does “They” mean?\",\"The treehouses.\",\"In “They are near the beautiful Diamond Beach”, what does “They” mean? The treehouses.\",\"\",[\"The beaches.\",\"The cities.\",\"The trains.\",\"The treehouses.\"],\"Treehouses are a lot of fun, but do you want to live in one? In Bali, Indonesia, you can try living in the famous Rumah Pohon Treehouse. There are three treehouses there that you can stay in. They are near the beautiful Diamond Beach.\",\"\"]","pattern_key":"exam-reading","title_th":"หาหลักฐานในข้อความ","rule_th":"อ่านคำถามว่าถามใคร ที่ไหน จำนวน วิธี หรือความหมาย แล้วหาใจความที่ตอบเรื่องเดียวกันในข้อความ","clue_th":"They ย้อนถึง three treehouses ในประโยคก่อนหน้า","caution_th":null,"contrasts":[{"label_th":"รูปแบบแรก","text":"Where? → a place"},{"label_th":"อีกตัวอย่าง","text":"How many? → a number"}],"examples":["In “They are near the beautiful Diamond Beach”, what does “They” mean? The treehouses.","Where is the house? → In Serbia."]},{"question_id":"exam-ch34-v1-reading-houses-rocks-assessment-transfer","content_key":"[\"sentences\",\"Which statement matches how the cave houses were made?\",\"People built homes inside rocks.\",\"Which statement matches how the cave houses were made? People built homes inside rocks.\",\"\",[\"People built homes above the sea.\",\"People built homes inside rocks.\",\"People built rocks inside trains.\",\"The houses were made from trees.\"],\"In Cappadocia, Turkey, you can find very different houses! Cappadocia has many cave houses. People made them inside large rocks. The rocks in Cappadocia are kind of soft. People have lived in these cave homes for thousands of years.\",\"\"]","pattern_key":"exam-reading","title_th":"หาหลักฐานในข้อความ","rule_th":"อ่านคำถามว่าถามใคร ที่ไหน จำนวน วิธี หรือความหมาย แล้วหาใจความที่ตอบเรื่องเดียวกันในข้อความ","clue_th":"made them inside large rocks: them คือบ้านถ้ำ ไม่ใช่ต้นไม้","caution_th":null,"contrasts":[{"label_th":"รูปแบบแรก","text":"Where? → a place"},{"label_th":"อีกตัวอย่าง","text":"How many? → a number"}],"examples":["Which statement matches how the cave houses were made? People built homes inside rocks.","Where is the house? → In Serbia."]},{"question_id":"exam-ch34-v1-reading-train-name-assessment-transfer","content_key":"[\"sentences\",\"Which city calls its overhead train the L?\",\"Chicago.\",\"Which city calls its overhead train the L? Chicago.\",\"\",[\"Bali.\",\"Cappadocia.\",\"Chicago.\",\"Tokyo.\"],\"In Chicago, the overhead train is called the L. The tracks make a loop around the city center and then run out in all directions to the different parts of the city. The tracks are supported by massive steel columns.\",\"\"]","pattern_key":"exam-reading","title_th":"หาหลักฐานในข้อความ","rule_th":"อ่านคำถามว่าถามใคร ที่ไหน จำนวน วิธี หรือความหมาย แล้วหาใจความที่ตอบเรื่องเดียวกันในข้อความ","clue_th":"In Chicago ระบุเมืองที่รถไฟเหนือถนนมีชื่อ the L","caution_th":null,"contrasts":[{"label_th":"รูปแบบแรก","text":"Where? → a place"},{"label_th":"อีกตัวอย่าง","text":"How many? → a number"}],"examples":["Which city calls its overhead train the L? Chicago.","Where is the house? → In Serbia."]},{"question_id":"exam-ch34-v1-reading-train-support-assessment-transfer","content_key":"[\"sentences\",\"Why are the steel columns mentioned?\",\"They hold up the tracks.\",\"Why are the steel columns mentioned? They hold up the tracks.\",\"\",[\"They drive the taxis.\",\"They form the river.\",\"They hold up the tracks.\",\"They sell train tickets.\"],\"In Chicago, the overhead train is called the L. The tracks make a loop around the city center and then run out in all directions to the different parts of the city. The tracks are supported by massive steel columns.\",\"\"]","pattern_key":"exam-reading","title_th":"หาหลักฐานในข้อความ","rule_th":"อ่านคำถามว่าถามใคร ที่ไหน จำนวน วิธี หรือความหมาย แล้วหาใจความที่ตอบเรื่องเดียวกันในข้อความ","clue_th":"supported by บอกหน้าที่รองรับราง ไม่ใช่หน้าที่ขายตั๋ว","caution_th":null,"contrasts":[{"label_th":"รูปแบบแรก","text":"Where? → a place"},{"label_th":"อีกตัวอย่าง","text":"How many? → a number"}],"examples":["Why are the steel columns mentioned? They hold up the tracks.","Where is the house? → In Serbia."]},{"question_id":"exam-ch34-v1-reading-train-platform-assessment-transfer","content_key":"[\"sentences\",\"A rider cannot climb stairs. What alternative does the passage give?\",\"Take an elevator.\",\"A rider cannot climb stairs. What alternative does the passage give? Take an elevator.\",\"\",[\"Swim to the platform.\",\"Take a plane to the platform.\",\"Take an elevator.\",\"There is no other way.\"],\"Riding the train is easy. Riders climb stairs or take an elevator from the sidewalk to the platform. They buy a ticket, go through a gate, and wait for the next train to take them where they want to go. A train ticket costs less than a taxi ride. At busy times, trains come as often as every ten minutes. At night and on weekends, they do not come as often. Some trains run all the time, day or night.\",\"\"]","pattern_key":"exam-reading","title_th":"หาหลักฐานในข้อความ","rule_th":"อ่านคำถามว่าถามใคร ที่ไหน จำนวน วิธี หรือความหมาย แล้วหาใจความที่ตอบเรื่องเดียวกันในข้อความ","clue_th":"stairs or an elevator มีอีกทางเลือกคือลิฟต์","caution_th":null,"contrasts":[{"label_th":"รูปแบบแรก","text":"Where? → a place"},{"label_th":"อีกตัวอย่าง","text":"How many? → a number"}],"examples":["A rider cannot climb stairs. What alternative does the passage give? Take an elevator.","Where is the house? → In Serbia."]},{"question_id":"exam-ch34-v1-reading-train-price-assessment-transfer","content_key":"[\"sentences\",\"A rider chooses the cheaper of the two journeys described. Which should they choose?\",\"The train.\",\"A rider chooses the cheaper of the two journeys described. Which should they choose? The train.\",\"\",[\"Both are free.\",\"Both have the same price.\",\"The taxi.\",\"The train.\"],\"Riding the train is easy. Riders climb stairs or take an elevator from the sidewalk to the platform. They buy a ticket, go through a gate, and wait for the next train to take them where they want to go. A train ticket costs less than a taxi ride. At busy times, trains come as often as every ten minutes. At night and on weekends, they do not come as often. Some trains run all the time, day or night.\",\"\"]","pattern_key":"exam-reading","title_th":"หาหลักฐานในข้อความ","rule_th":"อ่านคำถามว่าถามใคร ที่ไหน จำนวน วิธี หรือความหมาย แล้วหาใจความที่ตอบเรื่องเดียวกันในข้อความ","clue_th":"less than หมายถึงน้อยกว่า รถไฟจึงถูกกว่าแท็กซี่ตามข้อความ","caution_th":null,"contrasts":[{"label_th":"รูปแบบแรก","text":"Where? → a place"},{"label_th":"อีกตัวอย่าง","text":"How many? → a number"}],"examples":["A rider chooses the cheaper of the two journeys described. Which should they choose? The train.","Where is the house? → In Serbia."]},{"question_id":"exam-ch34-v1-reading-train-frequency-assessment-transfer","content_key":"[\"sentences\",\"Compared with busy times, what should a weekend rider expect?\",\"Less frequent trains.\",\"Compared with busy times, what should a weekend rider expect? Less frequent trains.\",\"\",[\"Exactly the same frequency.\",\"Less frequent trains.\",\"No trains anywhere.\",\"Trains every ten seconds.\"],\"Riding the train is easy. Riders climb stairs or take an elevator from the sidewalk to the platform. They buy a ticket, go through a gate, and wait for the next train to take them where they want to go. A train ticket costs less than a taxi ride. At busy times, trains come as often as every ten minutes. At night and on weekends, they do not come as often. Some trains run all the time, day or night.\",\"\"]","pattern_key":"exam-reading","title_th":"หาหลักฐานในข้อความ","rule_th":"อ่านคำถามว่าถามใคร ที่ไหน จำนวน วิธี หรือความหมาย แล้วหาใจความที่ตอบเรื่องเดียวกันในข้อความ","clue_th":"do not come as often แปลว่าถี่น้อยลง ไม่ได้แปลว่าไม่มีรถไฟ","caution_th":null,"contrasts":[{"label_th":"รูปแบบแรก","text":"Where? → a place"},{"label_th":"อีกตัวอย่าง","text":"How many? → a number"}],"examples":["Compared with busy times, what should a weekend rider expect? Less frequent trains.","Where is the house? → In Serbia."]},{"question_id":"exam-ch34-v1-reading-houses-percent-assessment-transfer","content_key":"[\"sentences\",\"Does the passage claim all city residents live in apartments?\",\"No, it says many people.\",\"Does the passage claim all city residents live in apartments? No, it says many people.\",\"\",[\"It only discusses trains.\",\"No, it says many people.\",\"No, it says nobody.\",\"Yes, it says everyone.\"],\"Fifty-six percent of the world’s people live in cities. Many people in the city live in apartments. Others live around cities, in smaller towns called suburbs. There are many houses in the suburbs. Outside of cities and suburbs is the countryside. The countryside has a lot of space, so there are big houses and even farms. Houses, apartments, and farms are not the only places where people live. Some people live in really different houses!\",\"\"]","pattern_key":"exam-reading","title_th":"หาหลักฐานในข้อความ","rule_th":"อ่านคำถามว่าถามใคร ที่ไหน จำนวน วิธี หรือความหมาย แล้วหาใจความที่ตอบเรื่องเดียวกันในข้อความ","clue_th":"Many หมายถึงจำนวนมาก ไม่ใช่ทุกคน","caution_th":null,"contrasts":[{"label_th":"รูปแบบแรก","text":"Where? → a place"},{"label_th":"อีกตัวอย่าง","text":"How many? → a number"}],"examples":["Does the passage claim all city residents live in apartments? No, it says many people.","Where is the house? → In Serbia."]},{"question_id":"exam-ch34-v1-reading-houses-space-assessment-transfer","content_key":"[\"sentences\",\"What connects open space with farms in this paragraph?\",\"More space allows big houses and farms.\",\"What connects open space with farms in this paragraph? More space allows big houses and farms.\",\"\",[\"Cave rocks stop all farming.\",\"Cities have no people.\",\"Farms make all houses small.\",\"More space allows big houses and farms.\"],\"Fifty-six percent of the world’s people live in cities. Many people in the city live in apartments. Others live around cities, in smaller towns called suburbs. There are many houses in the suburbs. Outside of cities and suburbs is the countryside. The countryside has a lot of space, so there are big houses and even farms. Houses, apartments, and farms are not the only places where people live. Some people live in really different houses!\",\"\"]","pattern_key":"exam-reading","title_th":"หาหลักฐานในข้อความ","rule_th":"อ่านคำถามว่าถามใคร ที่ไหน จำนวน วิธี หรือความหมาย แล้วหาใจความที่ตอบเรื่องเดียวกันในข้อความ","clue_th":"so เชื่อมเหตุมีพื้นที่มากกับผลคือบ้านใหญ่และฟาร์ม","caution_th":null,"contrasts":[{"label_th":"รูปแบบแรก","text":"Where? → a place"},{"label_th":"อีกตัวอย่าง","text":"How many? → a number"}],"examples":["What connects open space with farms in this paragraph? More space allows big houses and farms.","Where is the house? → In Serbia."]},{"question_id":"exam-ch34-v1-reading-houses-water-assessment-transfer","content_key":"[\"sentences\",\"Which position should a drawing of the Drina River house show?\",\"Over the water.\",\"Which position should a drawing of the Drina River house show? Over the water.\",\"\",[\"Beside the water.\",\"Inside a cave.\",\"Over the water.\",\"Under the water.\"],\"The Drina River house is not a house beside the water. It’s a house over the water! This house is in Serbia. People love to visit and take photographs of it.\",\"\"]","pattern_key":"exam-reading","title_th":"หาหลักฐานในข้อความ","rule_th":"อ่านคำถามว่าถามใคร ที่ไหน จำนวน วิธี หรือความหมาย แล้วหาใจความที่ตอบเรื่องเดียวกันในข้อความ","clue_th":"ข้อความแก้จาก not beside เป็น over ต้องอ่านคำปฏิเสธด้วย","caution_th":null,"contrasts":[{"label_th":"รูปแบบแรก","text":"Where? → a place"},{"label_th":"อีกตัวอย่าง","text":"How many? → a number"}],"examples":["Which position should a drawing of the Drina River house show? Over the water.","Where is the house? → In Serbia."]},{"question_id":"exam-ch34-v1-reading-houses-bali-assessment-transfer","content_key":"[\"sentences\",\"Which pair of place and accommodation matches the passage?\",\"Bali — treehouses.\",\"Which pair of place and accommodation matches the passage? Bali — treehouses.\",\"\",[\"Bali — treehouses.\",\"Chicago — cave houses.\",\"Serbia — subway homes.\",\"Turkey — train platforms.\"],\"Treehouses are a lot of fun, but do you want to live in one? In Bali, Indonesia, you can try living in the famous Rumah Pohon Treehouse. There are three treehouses there that you can stay in. They are near the beautiful Diamond Beach.\",\"\"]","pattern_key":"exam-reading","title_th":"หาหลักฐานในข้อความ","rule_th":"อ่านคำถามว่าถามใคร ที่ไหน จำนวน วิธี หรือความหมาย แล้วหาใจความที่ตอบเรื่องเดียวกันในข้อความ","clue_th":"Rumah Pohon Treehouse อยู่ใน Bali, Indonesia","caution_th":null,"contrasts":[{"label_th":"รูปแบบแรก","text":"Where? → a place"},{"label_th":"อีกตัวอย่าง","text":"How many? → a number"}],"examples":["Which pair of place and accommodation matches the passage? Bali — treehouses.","Where is the house? → In Serbia."]},{"question_id":"exam-ch34-v1-reading-houses-soft-assessment-transfer","content_key":"[\"sentences\",\"In “The rocks in Cappadocia are kind of soft”, which thing has this quality?\",\"Rocks.\",\"In “The rocks in Cappadocia are kind of soft”, which thing has this quality? Rocks.\",\"\",[\"Passengers.\",\"Rocks.\",\"Steel columns.\",\"Train tickets.\"],\"In Cappadocia, Turkey, you can find very different houses! Cappadocia has many cave houses. People made them inside large rocks. The rocks in Cappadocia are kind of soft. People have lived in these cave homes for thousands of years.\",\"\"]","pattern_key":"exam-reading","title_th":"หาหลักฐานในข้อความ","rule_th":"อ่านคำถามว่าถามใคร ที่ไหน จำนวน วิธี หรือความหมาย แล้วหาใจความที่ตอบเรื่องเดียวกันในข้อความ","clue_th":"หา soft ขยายประธาน The rocks ไม่ใช่คนหรือรถไฟ","caution_th":null,"contrasts":[{"label_th":"รูปแบบแรก","text":"Where? → a place"},{"label_th":"อีกตัวอย่าง","text":"How many? → a number"}],"examples":["In “The rocks in Cappadocia are kind of soft”, which thing has this quality? Rocks.","Where is the house? → In Serbia."]},{"question_id":"exam-ch34-v1-reading-houses-years-assessment-transfer","content_key":"[\"sentences\",\"Which time scale describes living in these cave homes?\",\"Thousands of years.\",\"Which time scale describes living in these cave homes? Thousands of years.\",\"\",[\"A few minutes.\",\"A single night.\",\"One school day.\",\"Thousands of years.\"],\"In Cappadocia, Turkey, you can find very different houses! Cappadocia has many cave houses. People made them inside large rocks. The rocks in Cappadocia are kind of soft. People have lived in these cave homes for thousands of years.\",\"\"]","pattern_key":"exam-reading","title_th":"หาหลักฐานในข้อความ","rule_th":"อ่านคำถามว่าถามใคร ที่ไหน จำนวน วิธี หรือความหมาย แล้วหาใจความที่ตอบเรื่องเดียวกันในข้อความ","clue_th":"for thousands of years ระบุระยะเวลาอย่างชัดเจน","caution_th":null,"contrasts":[{"label_th":"รูปแบบแรก","text":"Where? → a place"},{"label_th":"อีกตัวอย่าง","text":"How many? → a number"}],"examples":["Which time scale describes living in these cave homes? Thousands of years.","Where is the house? → In Serbia."]},{"question_id":"exam-ch34-v1-reading-train-noise-assessment-transfer","content_key":"[\"sentences\",\"What corrects the reader’s first impression of thunder?\",\"The next sentence identifies a passing train.\",\"What corrects the reader’s first impression of thunder? The next sentence identifies a passing train.\",\"\",[\"A taxi is making a phone call.\",\"The next sentence identifies a passing train.\",\"The passage says it is a rainstorm.\",\"The sun has disappeared.\"],\"The sun is shining, but you think you hear thunder. Look up! A train is passing over your head!\",\"\"]","pattern_key":"exam-reading","title_th":"หาหลักฐานในข้อความ","rule_th":"อ่านคำถามว่าถามใคร ที่ไหน จำนวน วิธี หรือความหมาย แล้วหาใจความที่ตอบเรื่องเดียวกันในข้อความ","clue_th":"อ่านประโยคต่อไปเพื่อแก้ความเข้าใจแรก เสียงมาจากรถไฟ","caution_th":null,"contrasts":[{"label_th":"รูปแบบแรก","text":"Where? → a place"},{"label_th":"อีกตัวอย่าง","text":"How many? → a number"}],"examples":["What corrects the reader’s first impression of thunder? The next sentence identifies a passing train.","Where is the house? → In Serbia."]},{"question_id":"exam-ch34-v1-reading-train-traffic-assessment-transfer","content_key":"[\"sentences\",\"How is the trains’ route different from the cars’ route?\",\"It is above the street traffic.\",\"How is the trains’ route different from the cars’ route? It is above the street traffic.\",\"\",[\"It is above the street traffic.\",\"It is behind every car.\",\"It is inside the buses.\",\"It is on the same road lane.\"],\"Some big cities build train tracks above the city streets. One of these cities is Chicago. On the ground, cars and buses start and stop in traffic. Above them, trains are moving from station to station with no traffic jams.\",\"\"]","pattern_key":"exam-reading","title_th":"หาหลักฐานในข้อความ","rule_th":"อ่านคำถามว่าถามใคร ที่ไหน จำนวน วิธี หรือความหมาย แล้วหาใจความที่ตอบเรื่องเดียวกันในข้อความ","clue_th":"Above them บอกระดับของรางแยกจากรถที่ติดบนพื้นถนน","caution_th":null,"contrasts":[{"label_th":"รูปแบบแรก","text":"Where? → a place"},{"label_th":"อีกตัวอย่าง","text":"How many? → a number"}],"examples":["How is the trains’ route different from the cars’ route? It is above the street traffic.","Where is the house? → In Serbia."]},{"question_id":"exam-ch34-v1-reading-train-loop-assessment-transfer","content_key":"[\"sentences\",\"Do the tracks stay only around the city center?\",\"No, they also reach other parts of the city.\",\"Do the tracks stay only around the city center? No, they also reach other parts of the city.\",\"\",[\"No, they also reach other parts of the city.\",\"They go only inside houses.\",\"They go only to the river.\",\"Yes, they never leave the center.\"],\"In Chicago, the overhead train is called the L. The tracks make a loop around the city center and then run out in all directions to the different parts of the city. The tracks are supported by massive steel columns.\",\"\"]","pattern_key":"exam-reading","title_th":"หาหลักฐานในข้อความ","rule_th":"อ่านคำถามว่าถามใคร ที่ไหน จำนวน วิธี หรือความหมาย แล้วหาใจความที่ตอบเรื่องเดียวกันในข้อความ","clue_th":"and then run out in all directions แสดงว่าไปส่วนอื่นต่อจากวงรอบ","caution_th":null,"contrasts":[{"label_th":"รูปแบบแรก","text":"Where? → a place"},{"label_th":"อีกตัวอย่าง","text":"How many? → a number"}],"examples":["Do the tracks stay only around the city center? No, they also reach other parts of the city.","Where is the house? → In Serbia."]},{"question_id":"exam-ch34-v1-reading-train-sequence-assessment-transfer","content_key":"[\"sentences\",\"Which order matches the passage?\",\"Ticket → gate → wait.\",\"Which order matches the passage? Ticket → gate → wait.\",\"\",[\"Gate → ticket → wait.\",\"Gate → wait → ticket.\",\"Ticket → gate → wait.\",\"Wait → ticket → gate.\"],\"Riding the train is easy. Riders climb stairs or take an elevator from the sidewalk to the platform. They buy a ticket, go through a gate, and wait for the next train to take them where they want to go. A train ticket costs less than a taxi ride. At busy times, trains come as often as every ten minutes. At night and on weekends, they do not come as often. Some trains run all the time, day or night.\",\"\"]","pattern_key":"exam-reading","title_th":"หาหลักฐานในข้อความ","rule_th":"อ่านคำถามว่าถามใคร ที่ไหน จำนวน วิธี หรือความหมาย แล้วหาใจความที่ตอบเรื่องเดียวกันในข้อความ","clue_th":"อ่านลำดับ buy a ticket, go through a gate, and wait","caution_th":null,"contrasts":[{"label_th":"รูปแบบแรก","text":"Where? → a place"},{"label_th":"อีกตัวอย่าง","text":"How many? → a number"}],"examples":["Which order matches the passage? Ticket → gate → wait.","Where is the house? → In Serbia."]},{"question_id":"exam-ch34-v1-reading-train-busy-assessment-transfer","content_key":"[\"sentences\",\"A train has just left at a busy time. Which stated interval describes frequent service?\",\"Every ten minutes.\",\"A train has just left at a busy time. Which stated interval describes frequent service? Every ten minutes.\",\"\",[\"Every ten days.\",\"Every ten minutes.\",\"Once a month.\",\"Once a year.\"],\"Riding the train is easy. Riders climb stairs or take an elevator from the sidewalk to the platform. They buy a ticket, go through a gate, and wait for the next train to take them where they want to go. A train ticket costs less than a taxi ride. At busy times, trains come as often as every ten minutes. At night and on weekends, they do not come as often. Some trains run all the time, day or night.\",\"\"]","pattern_key":"exam-reading","title_th":"หาหลักฐานในข้อความ","rule_th":"อ่านคำถามว่าถามใคร ที่ไหน จำนวน วิธี หรือความหมาย แล้วหาใจความที่ตอบเรื่องเดียวกันในข้อความ","clue_th":"as often as every ten minutes บอกความถี่ที่มีได้ ไม่ใช่รับรองทุกเที่ยว","caution_th":null,"contrasts":[{"label_th":"รูปแบบแรก","text":"Where? → a place"},{"label_th":"อีกตัวอย่าง","text":"How many? → a number"}],"examples":["A train has just left at a busy time. Which stated interval describes frequent service? Every ten minutes.","Where is the house? → In Serbia."]},{"question_id":"exam-ch34-v1-reading-train-students-assessment-transfer","content_key":"[\"sentences\",\"Which pair contains activities the passage gives for students?\",\"Homework and phone games.\",\"Which pair contains activities the passage gives for students? Homework and phone games.\",\"\",[\"Building tracks and farming.\",\"Cooking and driving the train.\",\"Homework and phone games.\",\"Selling cars and cleaning caves.\"],\"While drivers on the ground are stuck in traffic, riders on the L are on their way. Students can do their homework or play a game on their phone. People read or talk. Some even go to sleep and wake up when they reach their stop.\",\"\"]","pattern_key":"exam-reading","title_th":"หาหลักฐานในข้อความ","rule_th":"อ่านคำถามว่าถามใคร ที่ไหน จำนวน วิธี หรือความหมาย แล้วหาใจความที่ตอบเรื่องเดียวกันในข้อความ","clue_th":"Students can do their homework or play a game on their phone กล่าวทั้งสองกิจกรรม","caution_th":null,"contrasts":[{"label_th":"รูปแบบแรก","text":"Where? → a place"},{"label_th":"อีกตัวอย่าง","text":"How many? → a number"}],"examples":["Which pair contains activities the passage gives for students? Homework and phone games.","Where is the house? → In Serbia."]},{"question_id":"exam-ch34-v1-reading-train-some-assessment-transfer","content_key":"[\"sentences\",\"Which claim goes beyond “Some trains run all the time”?\",\"Every train runs all night.\",\"Which claim goes beyond “Some trains run all the time”? Every train runs all night.\",\"\",[\"At least some trains run at night.\",\"Every train runs all night.\",\"Some trains run day or night.\",\"Some trains run in the daytime.\"],\"Riding the train is easy. Riders climb stairs or take an elevator from the sidewalk to the platform. They buy a ticket, go through a gate, and wait for the next train to take them where they want to go. A train ticket costs less than a taxi ride. At busy times, trains come as often as every ten minutes. At night and on weekends, they do not come as often. Some trains run all the time, day or night.\",\"\"]","pattern_key":"exam-reading","title_th":"หาหลักฐานในข้อความ","rule_th":"อ่านคำถามว่าถามใคร ที่ไหน จำนวน วิธี หรือความหมาย แล้วหาใจความที่ตอบเรื่องเดียวกันในข้อความ","clue_th":"Some ใช้กับบางขบวน จึงสรุปเป็น every train ไม่ได้","caution_th":null,"contrasts":[{"label_th":"รูปแบบแรก","text":"Where? → a place"},{"label_th":"อีกตัวอย่าง","text":"How many? → a number"}],"examples":["Which claim goes beyond “Some trains run all the time”? Every train runs all night.","Where is the house? → In Serbia."]},{"question_id":"exam-ch34-v1-reading-train-main-assessment-transfer","content_key":"[\"sentences\",\"Which summary best combines travel and passenger activity?\",\"Passengers keep moving and can read, work or rest.\",\"Which summary best combines travel and passenger activity? Passengers keep moving and can read, work or rest.\",\"\",[\"Passengers cannot do homework.\",\"Passengers keep moving and can read, work or rest.\",\"Passengers must drive the train.\",\"Passengers must stop at every car.\"],\"While drivers on the ground are stuck in traffic, riders on the L are on their way. Students can do their homework or play a game on their phone. People read or talk. Some even go to sleep and wake up when they reach their stop.\",\"\"]","pattern_key":"exam-reading","title_th":"หาหลักฐานในข้อความ","rule_th":"อ่านคำถามว่าถามใคร ที่ไหน จำนวน วิธี หรือความหมาย แล้วหาใจความที่ตอบเรื่องเดียวกันในข้อความ","clue_th":"สรุปทั้งการเดินทางขณะถนนติดและกิจกรรมของผู้โดยสาร","caution_th":null,"contrasts":[{"label_th":"รูปแบบแรก","text":"Where? → a place"},{"label_th":"อีกตัวอย่าง","text":"How many? → a number"}],"examples":["Which summary best combines travel and passenger activity? Passengers keep moving and can read, work or rest.","Where is the house? → In Serbia."]},{"question_id":"exam-ch34-v1-grammar-under-apple","content_key":"[\"sentences\",\"The apple is _____ the box.\",\"under\",\"The apple is under the box.\",\"Place: under\",[\"above\",\"in\",\"on\",\"under\"],\"\",\"under\"]","pattern_key":"exam-grammar","title_th":"ดูตำแหน่งเทียบกับสิ่งอ้างอิง","rule_th":"หาสิ่งที่กำลังพูดถึงก่อน แล้วดูว่ามันอยู่ตรงไหนเมื่อเทียบกับกล่อง ไม่เลือกจากชื่อสิ่งของเพียงอย่างเดียว","clue_th":"แอปเปิลอยู่ต่ำกว่ากล่องและตรงกับกล่องในแนวดิ่ง ใช้ under","caution_th":null,"contrasts":[{"label_th":"รูปแบบแรก","text":"under the box"},{"label_th":"อีกตัวอย่าง","text":"on the box"}],"examples":["The apple is under the box.","The ball is under the box."]},{"question_id":"exam-ch34-v1-grammar-under-book","content_key":"[\"sentences\",\"The book is _____ the box.\",\"under\",\"The book is under the box.\",\"Place: under\",[\"above\",\"in\",\"on\",\"under\"],\"\",\"under\"]","pattern_key":"exam-grammar","title_th":"ดูตำแหน่งเทียบกับสิ่งอ้างอิง","rule_th":"หาสิ่งที่กำลังพูดถึงก่อน แล้วดูว่ามันอยู่ตรงไหนเมื่อเทียบกับกล่อง ไม่เลือกจากชื่อสิ่งของเพียงอย่างเดียว","clue_th":"หนังสืออยู่ต่ำกว่ากล่องและตรงกับกล่องในแนวดิ่ง ใช้ under","caution_th":null,"contrasts":[{"label_th":"รูปแบบแรก","text":"under the box"},{"label_th":"อีกตัวอย่าง","text":"on the box"}],"examples":["The book is under the box.","The ball is under the box."]},{"question_id":"exam-ch34-v1-grammar-under-cube","content_key":"[\"sentences\",\"The cube is _____ the box.\",\"under\",\"The cube is under the box.\",\"Place: under\",[\"above\",\"in\",\"on\",\"under\"],\"\",\"under\"]","pattern_key":"exam-grammar","title_th":"ดูตำแหน่งเทียบกับสิ่งอ้างอิง","rule_th":"หาสิ่งที่กำลังพูดถึงก่อน แล้วดูว่ามันอยู่ตรงไหนเมื่อเทียบกับกล่อง ไม่เลือกจากชื่อสิ่งของเพียงอย่างเดียว","clue_th":"ลูกบาศก์เล็กอยู่ต่ำกว่ากล่องและตรงกับกล่องในแนวดิ่ง ใช้ under","caution_th":null,"contrasts":[{"label_th":"รูปแบบแรก","text":"under the box"},{"label_th":"อีกตัวอย่าง","text":"on the box"}],"examples":["The cube is under the box.","The ball is under the box."]},{"question_id":"exam-ch34-v1-grammar-behind-apple","content_key":"[\"sentences\",\"The apple is _____ the box.\",\"behind\",\"The apple is behind the box.\",\"Place: behind\",[\"behind\",\"in\",\"in front of\",\"on\"],\"\",\"behind\"]","pattern_key":"exam-grammar","title_th":"ดูตำแหน่งเทียบกับสิ่งอ้างอิง","rule_th":"หาสิ่งที่กำลังพูดถึงก่อน แล้วดูว่ามันอยู่ตรงไหนเมื่อเทียบกับกล่อง ไม่เลือกจากชื่อสิ่งของเพียงอย่างเดียว","clue_th":"กล่องบังแอปเปิลไว้ แสดงว่าแอปเปิลอยู่ด้านหลัง ใช้ behind","caution_th":null,"contrasts":[{"label_th":"รูปแบบแรก","text":"behind the box"},{"label_th":"อีกตัวอย่าง","text":"under the box"}],"examples":["The apple is behind the box.","The ball is behind the box."]},{"question_id":"exam-ch34-v1-grammar-behind-book","content_key":"[\"sentences\",\"The book is _____ the box.\",\"behind\",\"The book is behind the box.\",\"Place: behind\",[\"behind\",\"in\",\"in front of\",\"on\"],\"\",\"behind\"]","pattern_key":"exam-grammar","title_th":"ดูตำแหน่งเทียบกับสิ่งอ้างอิง","rule_th":"หาสิ่งที่กำลังพูดถึงก่อน แล้วดูว่ามันอยู่ตรงไหนเมื่อเทียบกับกล่อง ไม่เลือกจากชื่อสิ่งของเพียงอย่างเดียว","clue_th":"กล่องบังหนังสือไว้ แสดงว่าหนังสืออยู่ด้านหลัง